Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-09-2001||06:53 PM||||I had the upper control arm bushing replaced, they told me after they finished that the bolt (drivers side)was worn a bit and I should replace that sometime when I can (they had none in stock) and the bushings were GM replacements..<P>After a few months driving, the drivers side is getting bad again, lots of play on the shaft, They wouldn't warranty it because of the bolt was worn, (they are out of business now).  I was looking closer at it tonight, the bushings seem tight and the play is in the bolt/shaft.   Can the bolts still be bought?  is there a special bolt for the fiero or should any dealer have a generic one in stock that would fit?  And if the bushing still looks good, would I still need to put a new one in if I just replace the bolt?<P>ALSO, what would cause just the drivers side bolt to get play in it? (passengers side is tight as if it was new) <P>Car was never hit, aligned regularly, etc..<BR>Thanks! <P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Bob Englert||06-09-2001||08:44 PM||||Is your car an 88 or pre-88?<P>The upper control arm bolts for the pre-88 are nothing special, just long hardened metric bolts.  You should be able to get them at any good fastener supply co.  Have you checked to see if you can still get them from GM?<P>The 88 upper control arm shaft is very unique to the car.  I think the Fiero Store is now stocking replacement shafts for the 88's.  <P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
